{"text":"{
  "status": "STABLE",
  "core_findings": [
    "Sampled training separation is strong: pairwise accuracy is 99.38% for Movies, 98.23% for Electronics and 99.10% for CDs, versus 92.07% for Industrial. These position-weighted estimates cover 11,841, 10,317, 15,963 and 11,076 valid positions respectively across ten batches per category; they do not measure held-out ranking or independent-user accuracy.",
    "Industrial endpoint representations are more concentrated: effective rank is 6.71 versus 26.83–28.16 elsewhere among 200 eligible identified training users per category, with similar results after unit normalization. Identity and batch-reordering checks pass with zero difference in all categories; uncertainty intervals for these representation statistics are not supplied."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "The model consistently separates sampled training positives from negatives, although Industrial has the highest negative-beats-positive rate at 7.93%.",
    "Industrial's concentration indicates fewer dominant representation directions, but does not establish defective representations or poor recommendation quality.",
    "Held-out ranking and temporal relevance effects remain unassessed: validation interventions are unavailable, and the supplied summary omits sensitivity effect sizes, control contrasts and intervals."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "Industrial_and_Scientific:pairwise_accuracy": 0.9207295052365475,
      "Industrial_and_Scientific:intact_user_endpoint_effective_rank": 6.71463969198642,
      "Industrial_and_Scientific:intact_user_endpoint_unit_normalized_effective_rank": 6.675762490129857,
      "Industrial_and_Scientific:intact_user_endpoint_leading_share": 0.39159267043598206
    },
    "brief_metric_read": {
      "pairwise_accuracy": "Separation conditional on sampled training-negative difficulty; no validation-quality inference.",
      "effective_rank": "Covariance concentration, not useful-ranking evidence; based on 200 eligible identified users per category.",
      "checks": "Identity and batch-reordering differences are zero; other omitted checks cannot be assessed.",
      "uncertainty": "Reported bootstrap methodology conditions on fitted models and fixed users/candidates; numerical intervals are omitted and exclude seed, candidate-sampling and search uncertainty."
    }
  }
}"}
